@title Summon Night - Swordcraft Story 2 (USA)
@file Summon Night - Swordcraft Story 2 (U).gba
@game BSKE
@chip EEPROM
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba
@known * audio differs from both references -- §57: the Rampage Rabbit fight's random numbers part all three emulators (no two share a frame f14401-f26400); the flagged audio is that stretch and its aftermath

# New Game, Edgar, keep the name, the opening on Cliff Road, the first battle
# (the Rampage Rabbit, won by mashing A towards it), Exeld named by default,
# back to Master's house, down to the workshop for Blaire's scene; the
# workshop's save crystal prompts "I should save the game": Save data? Yes,
# DATA 1 (Lv 2 Edgar, Workshop, 9:26). [load]: Continue, DATA 1, Load data?
# Yes, resumes beside the crystal in the workshop.
# Findings: the battle's random numbers differ in all three emulators: the
# three frames are identical at f13848 as it opens, yet by f13980 the rabbit
# stands somewhere else in each (small animations already differ before:
# mgba's sparkles at f4554, nba's dialogue text a few frames behind the
# other two from the character select on). The fight plays out differently
# in each: per-frame hashes match nowhere between any two emulators from
# f14401 to f26400, the rabbit falls at a different time in each and the
# following dialogue runs out of step (mashed A: the default name Exeld is
# confirmed in every emulator however many presses land on it). They
# re-converge in Master's house (f27000) and match again through the save,
# except for what the fight left: Edgar's HP (117/120/123 of 126 in
# dingbat/mgba/nba), so the three battery files differ in 6 bytes. dingbat's
# four configurations write byte-identical saves, and every save loads in
# every emulator. The audio check flags dingbat in 4% of windows: ten runs
# inside that out-of-step stretch (f14565-f26220, where it compares
# different moments of the game) and two short ones in the house
# (f29055, f29310), after a fight that ended at a different time in each.
